# Vercel only needs console/ (built per vercel.json's buildCommand) and api/
# (the serverless function, with its own minimal api/requirements.txt -- see
# api/index.py's module docstring). Everything else is the full local/dev
# project: real ML dependencies (numpy/scikit-learn/shap/river -- river pulls
# in llvmlite, which fails to build in Vercel's Python build sandbox), the
# real network-namespace testbed, tests, docs, research writeups. None of it
# belongs in the deployed function, and letting Vercel's framework
# auto-detection see the root pyproject.toml makes it try to build the whole
# thing as one FastAPI app instead of respecting vercel.json's own build/
# rewrite config -- this is what actually broke the first git-linked deploy
# (see decisions.md's dated entry).
# NOT argus/ wholesale: api/index.py genuinely imports argus.evidence.bundle,
# argus.evidence.replay, argus.respond.{guard,ladder}, argus.correlate.correlator,
# argus.risk.engine, argus.sim.devices, and argus.schemas at runtime -- all pure
# standard-library code with no ML dependency (see api/index.py's own module
# docstring, and docs/18-live-sensor.md section 5 for why the live-sensor
# ingest path specifically needs correlate/risk/respond/evidence). Excluding any
# of those broke a deploy before (first: ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
# 'argus'; again when argus/correlate, argus/risk, argus/sim, and
# argus/schemas.py were added to this file's exclusion list while the live-
# sensor endpoints were being built, without checking their new import graph
# against it -- FUNCTION_INVOCATION_FAILED on every route, caught before being
# reported as done, not after; see decisions.md). Exclude only the
# subpackages/files api/index.py's import graph never actually reaches.
argus/api/
argus/behavior/
argus/collector/
argus/data/
argus/db/
argus/detect/
argus/features/
argus/registry/
argus/respond/adapters/
# argus/sim/devices.py is needed (argus.risk.engine's FLEET criticality lookup);
# engine.py/attacks.py are the synthetic-scenario generator, never imported by
# api/index.py's own code.
argus/sim/engine.py
argus/sim/attacks.py
argus/testbed/
argus/verify/
argus/pipeline.py
# argus/control.py is the local-dev DB-backed command-queue implementation
# (needs argus.db.models -> SQLAlchemy); api/index.py has its own separate
# in-memory implementation of the same endpoints and never imports this file.
argus/control.py
compose/
data/
docs/
eval/
research/
resume/
results/
scripts/
tests/
pyproject.toml
uv.lock
Makefile
MASTER-PLAN.md
BUILD-ORDER.md
CLAUDE.md
STATUS.md
progress.md
decisions.md
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
*.egg-info/
